[center][size=6][b]HOLLOW HALLS PROGRESSION[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]R E T U R N   B E A C O N   T R A V E L[/color][/size]

[size=3]The Hollow Halls, one beacon at a time.[/size][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/272/272-1793420523-1425622793.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

The Hollow Halls are long, and leaving one halfway means starting over. This mod remembers every [b]Return Beacon[/b] you reach inside them, so you can stop whenever you like and pick up where you left off.
[list]
[*][b]Reach a Return Beacon[/b] in any of the six Hollow Halls: a notice tells you it's saved ("Return Beacon 2 of 5 reached").
[*][b]Click that Hollow Halls on the world map.[/b] Under Send Ping and Set as Waypoint there is a button for each Return Beacon you reached.
[*][b]Pick one:[/b] a loading screen with a picture of that hall shows while the area loads, and you arrive next to the beacon.
[*][b]Your choice on the server:[/b] beacons stay unlocked for good (default), or a hall's beacons reset once you finish it.
[*][b]In your language:[/b] the notices and the loading screen follow the game's language setting, in all 15 languages Enshrouded supports.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/272/272-1793420548-571358894.jpg[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/272/272-1793420555-1327784740.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\hollow-halls-progression[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game and walk up to a Return Beacon in a Hollow Halls.
[/list]

[b]Single player and hosting your own game:[/b] that's all. Your game is the host.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\hollow-halls-progression[/i]; if no other Greeneye mod is left, also [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Dedicated server[/b][/size]

On a dedicated server the mod has to be on the server [b]and[/b] on the game of every player who wants beacon travel. The server keeps everyone's beacons.
[list=1]
[*]Stop the server.
[*]Open the server folder, the one with [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i]. In Steam: Library > Tools > Enshrouded Dedicated Server > right-click > Manage > Browse local files. With SteamCMD it's the folder you installed to; with a rented server, use the host's file manager or FTP.
[*]Copy everything from the zip into that folder, the same way as for the game: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\hollow-halls-progression[/b] folder.
[*]Start the server.
[*]Check it loaded: [i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] in the server folder should contain [i]Hollow Halls Progression 1.0.0: server companion loaded[/i].
[/list]

[b]Players:[/b] each player installs the mod on their own game as described above. Players without the mod can still join and play; they just don't get beacon travel.

[b]Rented servers:[/b] the host must let you add files next to [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i]. Tested on a Windows server; not tested on Linux/Wine hosting.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[i]greeneye\hollow-halls-progression\hollow-halls-progression.ini[/i], each setting explained in the file. Restart the game (or the server) after changing it.
[list]
[*][b]ResetOnBossKill[/b] (host setting): [i]false[/i] keeps Return Beacons unlocked for good (default). [i]true[/i] resets a player's beacons in a hall once they finish it: when one of the hall's end chests (the warrior, ranger and mage gear at the end) is looted while they are inside.
[*][b]ShowNotices[/b] and [b]Language[/b] (each player's own): whether notices are shown, and in which language.
[/list]

The host (the dedicated server, or your game when you play alone or host) keeps each player's beacons in [i]progress.txt[/i] in the same folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The notices and the loading screen come in every language the game supports: English, French, Italian, German, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian and Thai. They follow the language set in the game. The beacon buttons use the game's own word for Return Beacon.

The translations were made with AI. If a line reads oddly in your language, please post a better one in the comments.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosting your own game, and dedicated servers[/b] (install it on the server too). Players without the mod can share the server and notice nothing.
[*]On a server without the mod, beacons aren't saved and the map shows no beacon buttons; nothing shows up in chat. Servers with text chat turned off work too.
[*]Progress is kept per player (Steam account) on the host. A host that runs several worlds shares one list across them.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit, Embervale Teleport, Town Portals and The Worst Map Mod), and chains onto hooks other mods put on the same game functions.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. After an update the mod checks that it still recognises the game; if it does not, it switches the affected parts off instead of risking a crash.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these with your report:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] in the game folder: what the Greeneye Loader and the mod did (the mod's lines start with "Hollow Halls Progression:").
[*]On a dedicated server, also [i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] from the server folder.
[*]If beacons go missing: [i]greeneye\hollow-halls-progression\progress.txt[/i] from the host (the server, or the game that hosts).
[/list]

